# U-Boot environment location for the Caddx Ascent Lite (Hi3516CV610).
#
# This file was entirely missing before — checked the whole builder and
# firmware trees, no device anywhere ships one — which is why every boot
# log showed "Cannot open config file '/etc/fw_env.config': No space left
# on device" (fw_printenv/fw_setenv failing outright, not misconfigured).
#
# The partition location is confirmed from a live boot log's "Creating 10
# MTD partitions" listing: 0x000000080000-0x000000100000 : "env" (mtd1,
# 512KiB absolute offset 0x80000). The size/sector values below are NOT
# guessed — they're read straight from the actual U-Boot this board runs,
# ~/Dokumente/fpv/OpenIPC/u-boot-hi3516cv6xx, configs/
# hi3516cv610_ascentfb3_defconfig (branch ascentfb3-custom):
#   CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET=0x80000       (matches the "env" partition start)
#   CONFIG_ENV_SIZE=0x10000         (64KiB — NOT the 128KiB NAND eraseblock)
#   CONFIG_ENV_SECT_SIZE=0x10000    (64KiB; that defconfig also carries
#                                    CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_SPI_FLASH — this unit
#                                    is the NAND variant, per the SPI-NOR
#                                    probe failing in the kernel boot log)
# No CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET_REDUND anywhere in that defconfig: single-copy env,
# matching the single "env" partition (no "env1").
#
# Still worth a read-only `fw_printenv` check before ever trusting
# `fw_setenv` to write here: confirm it shows real values (whatever's
# actually been `setenv` from U-Boot — usbnet_ip, ipaddr, etc.), not
# CRC-garbage or nothing, in case that defconfig drifts from what's
# actually flashed.
#
# MTD device      Device offset   Env size   Flash sector size   Number of sectors
/dev/mtd1         0x0000          0x10000    0x10000             8
